 {"id": "TJ-REVIEW-074", "title": "[P4] auto-sandbox (modify) rewrites bypass the wrapper's own namespace preflight: on a host where the rewrite's unshare prefix is denied the payload dies inside the sandbox tail with a raw interpreter error (observed: '/home/kara/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python3: Permission denied', rc=126) — the documented 'auto-sandbox modify unavailable' verdict did not fire", "status": "pending", "priority": "P4", "created_at": "2026-10-21T21:41:29Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-22T03:44:42Z", "created_by": null, "capability_tags": ["auto-sandbox", "modify-path", "fail-attribution"], "complexity": 3, "attempts": 0, "blocks": [], "blocked_reason": null, "depends_on": [], "created_by_note": null, "reasoning": "Hands-on review 2026-10-21 @ 02d876f5, this host (AppArmor denies bare unshare, allows userns; auto backend=bwrap). './standalone/terminal-jail pytest --version' -> verdict modify/auto-pytest (yaml layer), rewrite 'unshare --user --pid --fork --kill-child=SIGKILL bash -c python3 <landlock-loader> -- pytest --version', then rc=126 with 'bash: line 1: /home/kara/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python3: Permission denied' (the payload's PATH python3 is unreadable under the mapping-less uid inside the rewrite's user namespace; the file is a 0755-dir/0777-symlink chain the mapped payload cannot traverse). quickstart.md:147-152 promises the wrapper PROBES the rewrite's own prefix and fails with an 'auto-sandbox modify unavailable' verdict naming the flags when the host cannot create it — here the prefix IS creatable (unshare --user --pid --fork succeeds rc=0 raw) but the composed launch still cannot run the payload, so no contract covers this state: the user sees a raw interpreter permission error from inside the jail, not a named-cause verdict. Sibling of DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-15 (payload=caller's subuid cannot read caller files on MAPPING hosts) and TJ-DF-050 (loader readability on the modify path): this is the MAPPING-LESS variant — the launch comes 